## Copy and Tone
- Direct, honest, slightly playful — never corporate
- "Ranked by people who actually own them" — ownership and authenticity matter
- No superlatives in UI copy ("amazing", "incredible", "best ever")
- Error messages explain what happened and what to do next
- Empty states invite action, never just say "nothing here"
- CTAs are specific: "Start voting" not "Get started", "Save to list" not "Save"

---

## Key UX Rules
- Search bar is always the most prominent interactive element
- Voting never requires a page reload — optimistic UI updates
- Buy buttons always open in a new tab
- Sign up modal appears on any action requiring auth — never a hard redirect
- Horizontal scroll rows always have a subtle right fade to hint at more content
- Mobile bottom sticky bar for Buy button on product detail page
- Tier bars from the logo appear as decorative accents in empty states and auth pages
- Pagination over infinite scroll on ranked list pages (better for SEO)
- Loading states on every async action — no blank flashes

---

## SEO Rules
- Every category page and product page gets unique meta title and description
- Category page title format: "Best [Category] — Ranked by the Community | Stier"
- Product page title format: "[Product Name] by [Brand] — [Tier] Tier | Stier"
- Static generation where possible, ISR for ranked lists (revalidate every hour)
- Canonical URLs on all pages
- OG image for social sharing on category and product pages

